  "id": "Compound::DB01151 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Desipramine is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c19 through a complex network of interactions involving other enzymes and pathways. The evidence suggests that Desipramine binds to Cyp2a6 and Cyp2e1, which both participate in the same metabolic pathway—Arachidonic Acid Monooxygenase Activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Cyp2c19, indicating a potential shared functional role in lipid metabolism. Additionally, the indirect pathway through Perphenazine, which binds to Cyp2c19, provides an alternative route for Desipramine to influence Cyp2c19, though this route is less direct. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Desipramine may modulate Cyp2c19, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a role for Desipramine in influencing Cyp2c19 through enzyme-mediated pathways, but the precise mechanism requires further investigation.",
